From: c4pp4
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 05:39:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] Fix playlist parsing, album art, filters, actions and
 translations

Playlists:
- skip the playlist title line instead of the fixed length of
  "title=Library"
- skip streams (e.g. internet radios), which were added as tracks
  without a file, and tracks already found in another playlist
- reset the track fields for each track, a track without a tag got the
  value of the previous track
- use the file name as title of a track without the title tag and skip
  tracks without an album in the Albums category
- return no results without the Audacious playlists, the scope is
  installed also without Audacious and failed at every search

Album art:
- read the embedded album art with mutagen from ID3 (MP3), FLAC, MP4
  and Ogg (Vorbis, Opus) files, the file name was cut by 7 characters
  and the ID3 picture was looked up by a wrong key
- look up the album art once per album and only for the shown results
- use the icon name in the preview when the album art is missing
  (file://media-audio failed in the Dash)

Search:
- return at most 100 songs and 100 albums without a search string, 20
  in the global search and 50 in the lens search as the Rhythmbox
  scope, all tracks of the library (thousands) were returned when the
  lens was opened
- look up the already added results in sets, the list lookups took
  seconds with a large library

Filters:
- add the Decade and Genre filters of the music lens, the filter state
  is passed only for the scope's own filters, so the search failed
  ("Unable to find filter with id") when a filter was used
- filter by the year and by the genre mapped to the filter options as
  in the Rhythmbox scope, "Old" means before 1960

Actions:
- show the track (the first track of an album) in the file manager via
  UnityExtras.show_in_folder(), the album action failed on a wrong
  variable and xdg-open was run via shell
- run Audacious without a shell, file names with an apostrophe broke
  the command line
- match album tracks by the exact album and artist name

Translations:
- the scope has no translations, use the same strings of the music
  lens (Play, Show in Folder, Songs, Albums)

Signed-off-by: c4pp4
